\p{"Its own" counts the inputs on which the published build gives the official verdict. "Reached the mode": the counter \code{\verb~|machine.let.units~} of the plain run is above 0. A plain run of the candidate never declined and never ended with an error. The two probes of section 4 (RV2B-F5) are in the second row.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3. The generator}

\p{The environment of every generated export is the triple of package S that the rows of MO-2 use: \code{\verb~|d (x : True /\ True) : Nat := And.rec (fun _ _ => 5) x~}, an axiom \code{h}, so that \code{\verb~|d intro~} is officially convertible with \code{5} and with \code{\verb~|d h~}, and \code{\verb~|d h~} is not convertible with \code{5}; and an axiom \code{\verb~|c : Nat~}, convertible with nothing else. A \em{type code} is two of the atoms \code{i} (\code{\verb~|d intro~}), \code{h} (\code{\verb~|d h~}), \code{5}, \code{c}: \code{\verb~|T(ab)~} is the K type at \code{a} with index \code{b}. The K rule fires on a major premise of type \code{\verb~|T(ab)~} iff \code{a} and \code{b} are officially convertible: \code{\verb~|T(ii)~} and \code{\verb~|T(i5)~} fire, \code{\verb~|T(h5)~} and \code{\verb~|T(5h)~} do not, and all four are pairwise convertible where no position sets \code{h} against \code{5}. \code{\verb~|R M~} is the K recursor into \code{Nat} with minor premise 7 on the major premise \code{M}; \code{\verb~|needs7 R~} is \code{\verb~|(fun (_ : R = 7) => True.intro) (Eq.refl 7)~}; \code{\verb~|P : Nat -> Prop~} and \code{\verb~|W : forall x, P (R (M x))~} are axioms, \code{\verb~|pf7 t~} is \code{\verb~|(fun (_ : P 7) => True.intro) t~}.}

\p{\strong{The model, and how far it held.} The generator predicts every verdict from one rule: inside \code{infer_let} a let variable has its declared type; after it the value term is substituted and typed in infer-only mode; a redex is typed through its binder, a let term through its let, a projection through its struct, a constant application through the constant's type. The prediction is a label only; the verdict that counts is the official one. The official checker agreed with the prediction on 10,545 of the 10,579 generated exports; the 34 others are a flaw of the model in one flavour (a stuck declared type in a checked position), not of the kernel's reading.}

\p{\strong{Kinds.} Every statement of the generator but those at the opaque index is derivable in the theory whatever the official checker says: \code{\verb~|d h~} and \code{5} are convertible in the theory (proof irrelevance and transitivity), so the K rule under any reading is definitional proof irrelevance (the argument of section 7.1 of the report of the package). An accept of an official reject on such an input is of kind T. At the opaque index no reading fires and the statement is not derivable: an accept there would be of kind F. 1,064 inputs are of that kind; the official checker rejects each of them because the recursor application does not reduce, not for a type error elsewhere.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Family}\th{What varies}\th{Exports}\th{Official accept / reject}\th{Candidate: official verdict}\th{rejections of accepts: own / shared}\th{accepts of rejects: own / shared}\th{Machine alone declines: candidate (base)}}
\tr{\td{g1, one let}\td{K type (\code{Eq}; a K type of the export with one index, with two indices, universe polymorphic); the binder (a proof, a function, a function with two arguments, an axiom as the value, a pair, a constructor pair, a function into a pair, a pair of a function); 20 shapes of the major premise; 8 flavours of the two types (declared fires only, value fires only, both, neither, a constructor as the value, the opaque index, a stuck type on either side); 11 positions of the comparison (inside, under a binder, in the type of a second let, through the type of \code{W}, after the let, as an argument, both states in one body, two lets with one binder)}\td{2,709}\td{1,354 / 1,355}\td{2,419}\td{12 / 180}\td{16 / 82}\td{546 (640)}}
\tr{\td{g2, two lets}\td{13 chains (alias, alias of a function, lambda body, partial application, a redex and a let term as the value, a projection, three lets, a beta-redex binder in either place); the firing pattern of the three types; 7 positions with the inner let left and bound again}\td{896}\td{352 / 544}\td{896}\td{0 / 0}\td{0 / 0}\td{99 (180)}}
